# Python and tooling
.venv/
**/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# Secrets: local settings and API keys (template: .env.example)
.env

# Logs (dataset generation, eval runs, servers, model conversion)
*.log

# Data: early generation attempts (the dataset is data/eval_raw.jsonl)
data/old/

# Results: tracked are everything the README points readers to, all written by `make results`:
#   per-query predictions results/*.jsonl, results/tuned_settings.json, the main tables
#   results/results_{eval,dev}.{md,json}, results/mcnemar_*.txt, the per-run eval reports
#   results/report_eval_*.md, and the latency benchmarks results/bench/.
# Ignored: orchestration scripts of past long runs, ad-hoc per-run tables (`make dev/eval`),
# ad-hoc reports (`make report SPLIT=dev`) and report side files.
results/*.sh
results/results_*_*.md
results/results_*_*.json
results/report_*.md
!results/report_eval_*.md
results/*.metrics.json
results/compare_*.md

# Models, servers and caches live outside the repo (~/sidm-models, ~/.ollama); see `make doctor`.
